courts-completed-case-timeliness-length-.d:
This is a 5 Year Location Report by court level, division and class, as represented in the Courts Dashboard.

• "Provincial Court Criminal Cases by Length of Time to Conclude" is a timeliness measure for the percentage of concluded criminal court cases by age category in Provincial Court.

• This report indicates the proportion of Provincial Court criminal concluded cases that have a time to conclusion within the following age categories:

o 1 to 60 days;

o 61 to 120 days;

o 121 to 180 days;

o 181 to 240 days;

o 241 to 365 days;

o greater than 365 days.

• The extracts report Provincial Court concluded case data for courthouses across BC.

• Fiscal Year datasets are available and are based on the date the case is concluded.

