geophysical.d:
Geophysical data for British Columbia can be obtained from three agencies:

1. BC Geological Survey: search the Publication Catalogue for released geophysical data and Assessment Reports for geophysical survey results from exploration activity;
2. Geological Survey of Canada: search GEOSCAN for geophysics in British Columbia and the Geoscience Data Repository for Geophysical Data;
3. Geoscience BC: has geophysical publications and data from surveys conducted since 2005.

leading-group-for-the-cariboo-region.d:
####Leading Group for the Cariboo Region (pinegroup or firgroup). ####

1. IDF - Fir Group: includes all forest polygons in NDT 4 (IDF and BG biogeoclimatic zones) that meet any of the following criteria:
*a) Douglas-fir ( Fd or Fdi) leading or ponderosa pine leading;
*b) Lodgepole pine leading, and Douglas-fir ( Fd or Fdi) or ponderosa pine greater than 15% in any inventory layer;
*c) Trembling aspen leading, and Douglas-fir ( Fd or Fdi) or Ponderosa pine greater than 15% in any inventory layer, and spruce, red-cedar, cottonwood and birch less than 6% in any inventory layer;
*d) No species information in inventory data (usually NSR stands), and inventory type group for pre-harvest stand or the current stand = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 29, or 32 These inventory type groups correspond to the following species compositions F, FC, FCy, FH, FS, FPl, Fpy, FL, FDEcid, PlF and Py. If inventory type group=0 and pre-harvest inventory type is not available, classify the polygon as Pine Group.

2. IDF-Pl Group: includes all forest polygons in NDT 4 (IDF and BG biogeoclimatic zones) that do not meet the above definition for IDF-Fir Group.

slope-aspect-categories-in-mule-deer-win.m:
[Slope_Category] is based on the slope percentage from 25m raster slope tiles.
- Flat: 0-10% slope
- Moderate: 11-30% slope
- Steep: 31-60% slope
- Very Steep: >60% slope

[Aspect_Category] is based on aspect degree from 25m raster aspect tiles.
- Cool: 316-60 degrees
- Moderate: 271-315 degrees or 61-135 degrees
- Warm: 136-270 degrees

[Slope_Aspect_Category] is derived from the [Slope_Category] and [Aspect_Category] fields. Values range from 1-10.
- 1: Slope_Category = Flat & Aspect_Category = any value;
- 2: Slope_Category = Moderate & Aspect_Category = Cool;
- 3: Slope_Category = Steep & Aspect_Category = Cool;
- 4: Slope_Category = Very Steep & Aspect_Category = Cool;
- 5: Slope_Category = Moderate & Aspect_Category = Moderate;
- 6: Slope_Category = Steep & Aspect_Category = Moderate;
- 7: Slope_Category = Very Steep & Aspect_Category = Moderate;
